    "solutionSteps": [
      "Mark midpoints M₁, M₂ and M₃.",
      "Construct perpendiculars to AB and BC through M₁ and M₂.",
      "Label their intersection O.",
      "Use the perpendicular-bisector theorem to conclude OA = OB = OC."
    ],
    "expectedResult": "The perpendicular bisectors meet at circumcenter O, which is equidistant from A, B and C.",
    "teacherNotes": "Invite students to explain why the visual and symbolic results agree.",
